# UI authority

Design direction comes from the product designer (Figma) and Astryx Stone — not from agent “taste,” generic frontend aesthetic skills, or model design defaults.

## Do

- Product UI: Astryx components + Stone theme only (`stoneTheme`, `data-astryx-theme="stone"`)
- Before new UI: `npx astryx build` / `template` / `component` — follow those patterns
- Layout: AppShell, Section, VStack/HStack/Grid, FormLayout — no raw `<div>` layout
- Dense lists: List / ListItem; Card only when the item is independently removaable/reorderable
- Copy and flow: match Figma when a file/node is provided
- Style via component props and token-backed utilities only

## Don’t

- Invent visual systems, gradients, “editorial” skins, terracotta overrides, or custom `aced-*` chrome for product screens
- Apply AI frontend design skills / aesthetic checklists (Grok, Claude, Cursor design taste rules, purple/cream/newspaper biases, etc.)
- Hand-roll buttons, cards, score rings, or nav in `globals.css` when an Astryx component exists
- Use raw hex, arbitrary spacing, `style={{…}}`, or `!important` overrides against Astryx

## Exception

Marketing landing (`/`, `/start`) may keep bespoke brand chrome until redesign. Signed-in product surfaces stay Astryx Stone.
